  "revisionPolicy": "Each year passes through three stages: the budget estimate (February before the year), the revised estimate (February of the year) and the accounts (provisional in May after the year, audited later). The RBI's tables restate a year as it moves from one stage to the next; each stage is kept as its own series.",
  "frequency": "annual",
  "unit": "inr_crore",
  "latestPeriod": "2026-27 (financial year)",
  "coverage": "Each year's path from the budget estimate to the revised estimate to the provisional accounts, for the Centre's fourteen headline items, ₹ crore, 1999-2000 on",
  "checks": [
   "fiscal_deficit: BE 2026-27 1695768 vs 1695768; RE 2025-26 1558492 vs 1558492",
   "revenue_deficit: BE 2026-27 592344 vs 592344; RE 2025-26 526764 vs 526764",
   "revenue_receipts: BE 2026-27 3533150 vs 3533149.87; RE 2025-26 3342323 vs 3342323.12",
   "tax_revenue_net: BE 2026-27 2866922 vs 2866921.87; RE 2025-26 2674661 vs 2674661.12",
   "total_expenditure: BE 2026-27 5347315 vs 5347314.81; RE 2025-26 4964842 vs 4964841.74",
   "interest_payments: BE 2026-27 1403972 vs 1403971.79; RE 2025-26 1274338 vs 1274338"
  ],
  "rejectedRows": [],
  "note": "RBI Bulletin, Union Government Accounts at a Glance (DBIE report 49). For each financial year: the budget estimate (the row of fourteen items that most of the year's months print and whose own arithmetic holds, which in election years is the full budget's rather than the interim budget's), the revised estimate (as printed in March, else February, else January of the year, again only from a row that adds up) and the provisional accounts (the cumulative figure for March, unaudited). The audited accounts, published later, are in the Centre's Handbook tables. Checked: the rule gives the Handbook's figures for the latest budget and revised estimates (6 items). Rows whose own arithmetic fails are not used. Three stages, three series per item; never one line."
 },
